WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.501
The deal to pull the United States

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.102
back from a debt

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:02.769
cliff meets

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:05.405
its first big roadblock today at 3 p.m..

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:07.140
The House Rules Committee convenes.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.441
It is TBD.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.110
Whether the unhappy conservatives

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.111
on that panel

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.078
will have enough votes

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:13.446
to try to kill the Biden

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:14.814
McCarthy debt pact

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.716
at its first legislative stop.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:17.984
Hardliners say the deal

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.052
that gave Speaker McCarthy

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.520
the gavel back in January

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.454
included a promise

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.923
that any legislation needed all nine

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:24.657
Republican Rules

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:25.291
Committee votes

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.793
to make it to the full House.

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.128
McCarthy allies say

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.729
they don't remember it that way.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:30.397
This Washington

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:31.898
wrinkle puts the must pass deal

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.300
in some considerable early peril.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.235
The hardliners say

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.102
the compromise doesn't

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:36.870
cut enough spending.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.737
But listen to Speaker

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:38.838
McCarthy this morning.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.173
He says he got the better

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.409
of the president and the Republicans

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:43.076
should vote yes.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:45.512
We're actually going to

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.047
spend less money

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.782
this year than we spent last year.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:49.983
Read The Wall Street Journal

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.317
They say it's a very good bill.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.185
This is the biggest

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:54.521
cut in American history that we vote for.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.655
I'm not quite sure

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:56.823
what else they want to go.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:57.924
I think we've got to look at where

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.025
the victories are.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.960
We don't spend another 4 trillion.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.363
We we allow them to keep going forward

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:07.367
till January.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.170
Let's get straight up to Capitol Hill.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.439
CNN's Melanie Sloan is live for us there.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:12.739
Melanie,

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:13.840
the speaker says Republicans

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.407
should vote for it,

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.309
but he's got some trouble on his hands.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:16.943
Yeah, that's right.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.244
There is a lot of outrage

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.846
on the right here over this deal.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:20.880
They feel like

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:21.981
he essentially gave up

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.750
too much in these negotiations.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.751
And the House Freedom Caucus

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.252
is actually holding a press conference

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.421
right now to rally opposition

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.355
against this bill.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.090
But, John,

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.791
the two big questions right now are,

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.460
do they have the votes to be able

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.194
to block this

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.495
from even coming to the floor

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:36.830
or passing on the floor?

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.365
And is Kevin McCarthy's speakership safe

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:40.767
now on the first question?

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.202
It does not appear that they do

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:43.870
have the power to block this.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:44.771
The bill does

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:45.672
have to go through the House

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:47.040
Rules Committee later today

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.308
before it can get a floor vote.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.442
And there are three hard

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.743
line conservatives on that panel.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.045
That was part of the deal

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:53.146
that Kevin McCarthy made

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:53.980
to become speaker.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.448
But two of them, Ralph

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.050
Norman and Chip Roy, are signaling

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.751
they will vote against the rule.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:01:59.619
But one of them,

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.254
Thomas Massie, we are learning,

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.423
is expected to support the rule,

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.458
which means it will be able to advance

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.392
and get on to the floor.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.428
But on that second question, John,

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.629
whether Kevin McCarthy

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.097
speakership is safe.

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.832
That is a lot less clear.

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:13.133
The House

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.135
Freedom Caucus did have a call last night

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.102
where they talked

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:17.604
about their strategy moving forward

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.239
and how they're going to approach this.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:20.773
And while a lot of them

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.075
are against the idea

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:23.243
of using a tool known

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:24.711
as the motion to vacate

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:25.678
which would essentially force

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.747
a floor vote on ousting Kevin McCarthy,

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.016
it only takes one member to be able

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:30.750
to force that vote.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.551
And Congressman

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.553
Chip Roy is especially angry.

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:34.320
He told Glenn

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.221
Beck in an interview

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.156
on the radio moments ago

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.191
that this deal is a betrayal of the power

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:38.791
sharing agreement

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:39.659
that we put in place

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.227
among House Republicans.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:41.861
And he also said,

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:42.929
if we can't kill this bill,

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:45.031
then we're going to have to regroup

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.533
and figure out the whole leadership

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:47.300
arrangement again.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.501
So a clearest

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.436
path clear, clear threat there, John,

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.071
and potentially his speakership at risk.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.406
Well, stand by, because, Chip Roy,

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:54.574
you just mentioned speaking right now.

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:55.542
Let's listen.

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:57.577
Do we actually run on

00:02:57.577 --> 00:02:59.279
actually trying to change this place,

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:01.147
actually trying to secure the border,

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:01.915
actually saying

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:02.282
that we're going

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.183
to raise the debt ceiling,

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:05.118
maybe you should actually enact

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:07.320
fiscal reforms to do so.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.155
We did that.

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.890
We worked in good faith.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.058
Everybody sitting around

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:13.593
working around the table

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:14.994
to accomplish the objectives

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:16.229
the American people sent here to do.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.431
Unfortunately,

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:20.500
last week, there was a breach.

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:25.271
There was a breach in the structure

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:26.072
that we agreed

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.440
to put in place

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.976
to make sure that we are representing

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:32.612
the American people through this

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:36.316
heretofore united Republican conference.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:39.352
The Republican conference right now

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.554
has been torn asunder.

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:42.422
And we are working

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:44.691
hard to try to put it back together again

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:46.192
this weekend

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:48.361
by making sure that this bill

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.129
gets stopped.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.831
I want to be very clear,

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.132
not one Republican

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:55.802
should vote for this deal, not one.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.037
If you're out there watching this,

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.205
every one of my colleagues

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:00.740
will be very clear.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:03.376
Not one Repub can should vote

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:04.677
for this deal.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:07.247
It is a bad deal.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.482
No one sent us here

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.951
to borrow an additional $4 trillion

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:17.557
to get absolutely nothing in return.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.425
But at best,

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.060
if I'm being really generous,

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:24.631
a spending freeze for a couple of years.

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:26.599
That's it.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:29.068
That's about what you get.

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.370
And frankly,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.671
you're going to make things worse.

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.840
And my Democratic colleagues know it.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.542
That's why they're supporting it.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.978
That's why they're going around gleeful.

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:39.779
There's a reason

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.114
our Democratic colleagues support this.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:42.382
There's a reason that

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:44.517
Mitt Romney supports this.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.551
There's a reason that Bill

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.420
Kristol supports this.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.856
It's all the same stuff.

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:52.392
There's a reason that

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:53.226
our conservative

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:55.561
allies are opposing it roundly.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:57.530
The Club for Growth scoring against it,

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.598
the Heritage Foundation

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:00.667
scoring against it, FreedomWorks

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.135
scoring against it.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:04.304
Ron DeSantis publicly opposed.

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:05.972
President Trump said

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:07.273
he thought we should default

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:10.310
rather than pursue this kind of lunacy.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:11.344
At the end of the day,

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:12.845
the only person that would default in

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:16.082
this town is Joe Biden unless Republicans

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.717
default on the American dream

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.752
by voting for this bad bill.

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:21.054
That is why you're listening to that

00:05:21.054 --> 00:05:22.522
Congressman Chip Roy of Texas.

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:23.556
You see members of the Freedom

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:24.457
Caucus, the House Freedom

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:25.491
Caucus surrounding him.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:27.360
Kevin McCarthy had to negotiate with them

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.094
to become speaker.

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:29.195
And now Chip Roy right there

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:30.063
threatening that

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:31.264
if this debt deal the speaker

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:32.565
cut with the Biden White House,

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:34.033
if it is passed, he's

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:35.335
threatening to revisit

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:35.902
the speaker's

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:37.236
hold on the gavel with me

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.738
in studio to share the reporting

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:39.939
and their insights CNN's Dana

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:42.008
Bash, CNN's Nia-Malika Henderson

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:44.277
and Simon Kim of the Associated Press.

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:45.778
So there you have it right there.

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:46.245
Number one,

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.013
McCarthy appears

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.614
to have the votes at the moment

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.083
to get it out of the Rules Committee.

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:50.650
The question

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:52.852
is, as he sits in the speaker's office.

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:53.553
What calculation

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:54.287
is going through his mind?

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:55.121
Does he also thinking

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:56.889
can survive a challenge to his leadership

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:58.891
or does he have to yet again

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.460
accommodate the right

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:01.561
and stop his own deal?

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:03.830
That would be

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.131
really remarkable

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:07.767
because this is the most delicate

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:09.335
of balancing acts

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.070
that both leaders in both parties

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:11.571
have to do.

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:13.406
The president is doing the same thing.

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:14.574
It's just that

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:16.509
maybe they haven't been as vocal

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:17.477
this morning

00:06:17.477 --> 00:06:18.945
as they have been in the past

00:06:18.945 --> 00:06:20.513
with his the left flank.

00:06:20.513 --> 00:06:23.282
And what we're talking about here is

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:26.552
a true compromise in the sense that

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:27.987
there are

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:30.123
if all goes as planned

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:31.657
from the perspective of the White House

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:32.825
and the House speaker,

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:35.194
there will be no votes

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:36.529
on the left

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:38.664
and there will be no votes on the right.

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:40.566
And they're going to need

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:42.835
the majorities to be gotten

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:45.271
basically in the middle by Democrats

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:46.873
and Republicans.

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:48.174
The chip arrives at the world

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:49.175
are serious.

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:51.110
Obviously, you just heard him say that.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:52.545
I spoke to a senior

00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:54.580
Republican House member this morning

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.616
who said that the feeling among the House

00:06:56.616 --> 00:07:00.553
leadership is that there are not enough

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:02.355
people who want to quote unquote,

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:04.457
emasculate their leaders,

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:06.559
both the president and the speaker,

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:08.327
in order to take this down.

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:09.695
We'll see if that holds. Right.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:10.963
So a traditional Washington

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:12.598
deal, the left and the right are mad.

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:13.699
You have enough votes in the middle,

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:14.467
you pass it,

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:15.902
everybody grumbles and you move on.

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:17.570
What makes this more interesting is

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:18.571
just because

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:19.572
Speaker McCarthy, House

00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:21.507
Republicans, adopted the rule one.

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:22.575
One person, a chip.

00:07:22.575 --> 00:07:24.210
Roy, sounds like it's going to be him.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.478
Yeah, he can change his mind,

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:26.245
but he comes to the floor,

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:27.079
let's say they pass this

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:27.747
and he comes to the floor

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:28.614
at the end of the week,

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:30.116
says, I want to vacate the chair.

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:32.385
Is Kevin McCarthy like John Boehner,

00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:34.353
like Paul Ryan to fill,

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:34.987
you know, essentially

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:35.822
going to lose his job?

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:36.722
Different circumstances,

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.157
but because of flak on the right?

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:39.692
Listen, I mean, this was always the fear.

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:41.661
I mean, we all covered all the 15 rounds

00:07:41.661 --> 00:07:43.429
and finally made the speakership

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:46.098
and sort of the underlying story was

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:48.401
how tenuous his grasp

00:07:48.401 --> 00:07:49.802
on the speakership was.

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:51.504
And with this happening,

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:53.973
you see Chip Roy's very strong words.

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:54.674
He said you know,

00:07:54.674 --> 00:07:55.708
the Republican conference

00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:56.943
has been torn asunder.

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:57.577
Not one

00:07:57.577 --> 00:07:59.779
Republican should vote for this deal,

00:07:59.779 --> 00:08:00.379
he said.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:01.214
So he does

00:08:01.214 --> 00:08:03.216
look as he's at least setting himself up

00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:04.217
to be somebody

00:08:04.217 --> 00:08:04.984
who would try

00:08:04.984 --> 00:08:07.286
to get the speaker out of there.

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:09.255
Can he bring others along?

00:08:09.255 --> 00:08:09.455
I mean,

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:11.290
he certainly seemed to be having a call

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.359
to arms there for other Republicans

00:08:13.359 --> 00:08:14.660
to vote no on this deal.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:15.094
And say,

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:15.361
you know,

00:08:15.361 --> 00:08:15.962
there's a reason

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:18.731
why Democrats are happy with this deal.

00:08:18.731 --> 00:08:19.732
And so we'll see.

00:08:19.732 --> 00:08:21.300
I mean, this was always going to be

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.302
a perilous time for Kevin McCarthy.

00:08:23.369 --> 00:08:24.837
We see a point out to your point

00:08:24.837 --> 00:08:25.705
about call for arms.

00:08:25.705 --> 00:08:26.973
It was quite interesting.

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:27.874
Governor DeSantis

00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:28.941
did say over the weekend

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:29.675
if he were in the house,

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:30.643
he would propose this deal.

00:08:30.643 --> 00:08:31.577
He would vote against it.

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:32.945
Donald Trump hasn't said anything.

00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:33.946
He had Chip Roy quoting

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:34.280
what Donald

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.681
Trump said in the CNN town hall

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:37.083
before this deal was struck,

00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:37.650
that at some point

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:38.284
they're going to default.

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:39.785
I'm not president. I don't care.

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:40.920
That was Trump's flippant.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.154
It was just a flippant attitude.

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:42.722
I'm not president.

00:08:42.722 --> 00:08:43.656
I'm going to get blamed.

00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:44.590
Go ahead. And default.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:46.092
But Trump has said nothing

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:47.693
at this tenuous moment.

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:49.028
Donald Trump has a lot of sway

00:08:49.028 --> 00:08:49.896
over House Republicans.

00:08:49.896 --> 00:08:51.697
If he were to say something,

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:52.832
he could tip the scale either way,

00:08:52.832 --> 00:08:53.566
could he not?

00:08:53.566 --> 00:08:54.867
He definitely could.

00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:56.802
Which is why you hear

00:08:56.802 --> 00:08:57.837
Congressman Chip Roy

00:08:57.837 --> 00:08:58.304
bringing

00:08:58.304 --> 00:09:00.439
all of the outside opposition,

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:02.041
whether it's conservative outside

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:04.510
spending groups whether it's what

00:09:05.111 --> 00:09:06.178
the former president said

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:07.747
before the deal was finalized,

00:09:07.747 --> 00:09:08.648
whether it's

00:09:08.848 --> 00:09:09.849
Florida Governor

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:12.618
Ron DeSantis trying to drum up opposition

00:09:12.618 --> 00:09:14.053
against this deal.

00:09:14.053 --> 00:09:15.821
And you do see how Speaker

00:09:15.821 --> 00:09:16.589
McCarthy at

00:09:16.589 --> 00:09:19.959
least has to go on a really aggressive

00:09:20.192 --> 00:09:22.361
public relations messaging offensive.

00:09:22.361 --> 00:09:24.063
You hear him saying over and over

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:25.731
since this deal was announced

00:09:25.731 --> 00:09:27.600
that Democrats got no wins in this deal,

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:28.701
which is quite accurate.

00:09:28.701 --> 00:09:30.336
But that is what he and his lieutenants

00:09:30.336 --> 00:09:31.470
have to say

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.039
to try to convince you

00:09:33.039 --> 00:09:33.339
you weren't

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:34.073
probably never going

00:09:34.073 --> 00:09:35.975
to get a chip, Roy, on any sort of deal.

00:09:35.975 --> 00:09:38.010
I think we're kind of missing that point.

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:38.778
But those people

00:09:38.778 --> 00:09:40.212
who are kind of teetering

00:09:40.212 --> 00:09:41.314
on the edge of a

00:09:41.314 --> 00:09:41.948
yes or no

00:09:41.948 --> 00:09:43.015
in the Republican conference,

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:45.017
he really does have to work overdrive

00:09:45.017 --> 00:09:45.918
to convince them

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:46.986
that this is the best deal

00:09:46.986 --> 00:09:48.955
that you can get with a Democratic Senate

00:09:48.955 --> 00:09:50.423
and a Democratic president and.

